# Keeps the Docker build context small and prevents host-installed
# artifacts (built on whatever OS the developer is on) from being copied
# into the image and overwriting what the container installs for itself.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile copies the host's local
# node_modules straight into the container, clobbering the Linux-native
# one that `npm ci` just installed a step earlier — which is what causes
# broken or missing build output (e.g. a missing dist/main.js).

node_modules
dist
coverage

# Secrets should never be baked into an image — they're injected at
# container start time via docker-compose's env_file/environment instead.
.env
.env.*

.git
.gitignore
.vscode
*.log
npm-debug.log*
